WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.500
The least

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.135
developed nation in Asia

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.404
is waiting for vital aid.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:04.671
The U.N.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.739
says Myanmar's military

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.840
junta is holding up

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.174
humanitarian access

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:08.842
to communities

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.244
devastated by cyclone muka.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.645
Rescue groups are warning

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.547
of what they call a large scale

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.182
loss of life.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.384
CNN has been speaking

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:17.717
to people

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.352
who saw their homes and loved ones

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.621
swept away in Sunday's storm.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.624
Paula Hancocks brings us their story.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.431
It was one of the strongest

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.566
cyclones to ever hit Myanmar

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.603
and it hit the most vulnerable

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.171
and desperate

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.241
Temporary shelters in this Rohingya

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.343
refugee camp were destroyed.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.311
More than 400 people have died

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.012
and entire

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.580
villages have been wiped out,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.450
according to eyewitnesses.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.420
Those who survived

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.287
try to salvage

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.457
anything left of their homes.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.463
And lay to rest.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:07.434
Those who were lost to exhaustion already

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.935
lost his home once.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.637
Fleeing religious persecution

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.671
by Myanmar's military

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.307
ten years ago, leaving everything behind.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.943
He's now homeless again.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.812
Let me just show you

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.780
the situation over here.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.549
My home is completely destroyed.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.017
Some of the people

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.119
have already clear my area.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.587
He has been helping

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.289
search and rescue missions,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.491
looking for the bodies of his neighbors

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.526
and helping to bury the dead.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.128
My heart is very, very broken.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.363
I don't know how to mention in what

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.866
but when I see the dead bodies,

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.068
I can't control my tears.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.136
Myanmar's military

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.003
has been accused

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.172
of killing thousands of Muslim Rohingya

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.675
in a bloody and brutal crackdown.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.844
It's been described by the United Nations

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:51.811
as a genocide.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.747
About a million Rohingya

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:55.548
fled to neighboring

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:58.051
Bangladesh, starting in 2017.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.552
But hundreds of thousands

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.421
still live here in Myanmar.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.455
Many displaced

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.591
and in dire need of humanitarian aid.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.861
Abdul Hussein says he saw his wife

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.362
and three daughters

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.964
swept away by the water

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.966
as they tried to flee to safety.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.101
Honey, let's leave it to them and give.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.903
There are a lot of families like us

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.037
We need shelter.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.339
We have no food.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.940
We don't know what to do tonight.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.108
We eat for lunch.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.676
And what we will do tomorrow.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.212
We've just lost everything.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.314
Hussein shows us where he slept

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.182
with his surviving

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.418
children and grandchildren last night.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.887
Do you think there will be any help

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.422
coming from the military?

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.157
I don't believe

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.525
they will come to help us.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.993
I would just have to struggle to feed

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.860
the six members of my

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.861
family that are left.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.664
Myanmar's junta leader Min

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.265
Aung Hlaing,

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.699
visited the same hard

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.469
hit area Sittwe on Monday.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.971
He promised aid from the military,

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:52.705
but the U.N.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.008
and many international aid organizations

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.210
say they have been heavily restricted

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.778
from entering the country

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.712
and different to rule

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.782
since they seized power two years ago,

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.517
leaving the residents of Rakhine.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.252
Many living in camps

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.221
to fend for themselves.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.990
The storms completely destroyed our life

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.326
and bring us on the road again.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.963
Already vulnerable communities

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.132
hoping for help that may never come.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.501
Paula Hancocks, CNN.

